From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hero Siege Offline Toolkit <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Build Release|x64 optimised, and name the patch series in
 the log

Why: Upstream's Release|x64 configuration has compiled with optimisation
disabled since commit 9fae796 (the same commit that added the stack trace
to the error report), so every hook, every interface call a plugin makes
per frame and the whole error-report path run as unoptimised STL code.
The YYToolkit.dll this toolkit distributed from ForgePact v1.3.1 to
v1.3.16 was not built that way: its string pooling, section set and size
match a plain "cl /O2" build, which its NOTICE never recorded. This
patch makes the optimisation level an explicit, reviewable part of the
series instead of a property of whoever ran the compiler: MaxSpeed,
whole-program optimisation off (the distributed DLL had none), and the
exception model stated rather than inherited: HkYYError's frame holds C++
objects, and if the runner's YYError leaves it by unwinding they rely on
it. Whether it returns or unwinds is NOT verified - patch 0005's
returned= / dropped= counters are what the first launch reads it from.
It also writes one line at the top of YYToolkit.log naming this build and
the series revision, so a log can always be matched to its source - the
absence of exactly that is how a binary with undocumented changes stayed
in distribution.

Evidence: YYToolkit.vcxproj Release|x64 has Optimization=Disabled at the
pinned commit; upstream history shows the change in 9fae796 with no
stated reason. A plain "cl /O2 /std:c++latest /MD /LD /EHsc" build of the
previously documented tree is 894,976 bytes against the distributed
904,192; without /O2 it is 1,180,160. NOT verified: why upstream turned
optimisation off, and whether an optimised build of THIS series behaves
identically in game - that is what the launch gate in the hub README is
for. No frame-time effect of the optimisation level has been measured.

Fails-safe: A build-configuration change cannot fall back at run time.
If an optimised build misbehaves, drop this patch from the series: every
other patch builds and passes its host tests at upstream's setting too.

Log-markers: "Hero Siege patch series"

Upstream-status: not submitted. Upstream's setting is deliberate; this is
a Hero Siege distribution choice.

diff --git a/YYToolkit/YYToolkit.vcxproj b/YYToolkit/YYToolkit.vcxproj
index 1d750a8..213d08b 100644
--- a/YYToolkit/YYToolkit.vcxproj
+++ b/YYToolkit/YYToolkit.vcxproj
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
     <ConfigurationType>DynamicLibrary</ConfigurationType>
     <UseDebugLibraries>false</UseDebugLibraries>
     <PlatformToolset>v143</PlatformToolset>
-    <WholeProgramOptimization>true</WholeProgramOptimization>
+    <WholeProgramOptimization>false</WholeProgramOptimization>
     <CharacterSet>Unicode</CharacterSet>
   </PropertyGroup>
   <Import Project="$(VCTargetsPath)\Microsoft.Cpp.props" />
@@ -140,7 +140,8 @@
       <LanguageStandard>stdcpplatest</LanguageStandard>
       <RuntimeLibrary>MultiThreadedDLL</RuntimeLibrary>
       <AdditionalIncludeDirectories>$(ProjectDir)include;%(AdditionalIncludeDirectories)</AdditionalIncludeDirectories>
-      <Optimization>Disabled</Optimization>
+      <Optimization>MaxSpeed</Optimization>
+      <ExceptionHandling>Sync</ExceptionHandling>
       <MultiProcessorCompilation>true</MultiProcessorCompilation>
       <AdditionalOptions>/d1trimfile:"$(SolutionDir)\" %(AdditionalOptions)</AdditionalOptions>
     </ClCompile>
diff --git a/YYToolkit/source/ModuleMain.cpp b/YYToolkit/source/ModuleMain.cpp
index d95a652..ae6bdce 100644
--- a/YYToolkit/source/ModuleMain.cpp
+++ b/YYToolkit/source/ModuleMain.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,9 @@
 using namespace Aurie;
 using namespace YYTK;
 
+// Revision of the Hero Siege patch series this binary was built from.
+static const char* const g_HeroSiegeSeriesRevision = "hs.1";
+
 EXPORTED void ModuleOperationCallback(
 	IN AurieModule* AffectedModule,
 	IN AurieModuleOperationType OperationType,
@@ -49,6 +52,16 @@ EXPORTED AurieStatus ModulePreinitialize(
 	CmpCreateConsole();
 	CmpCreateLogFile("YYToolkit.log");
 
+	// This is not upstream's binary. Say so first, so every log names the
+	// source that produced it: upstream v4.0.1 plus the patch series kept in
+	// hero-siege-offline-toolkit under third_party/yytoolkit. Whoever changes
+	// the series bumps the revision.
+	CmWriteLogOutput(
+		"[hs] YYToolkit %d.%d.%d, Hero Siege patch series %s (hero-siege-offline-toolkit, third_party/yytoolkit)",
+		YYTK_MAJOR, YYTK_MINOR, YYTK_PATCH,
+		g_HeroSiegeSeriesRevision
+	);
+
 	AurieStatus last_status = AURIE_SUCCESS;
 
 	last_status = ObCreateInterface(
